   "title": "Canvas size",
   "properties": {
    "text": "",
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "CANVAS SIZE\n\ncanvas_mode decides the resolution H3 generates at:\n\n  manual            - use canvas_width/height exactly as typed\n  auto_no_downscale - size from the LARGEST crop in the clip, so no frame is\n                      ever downscaled. Can get expensive on clips containing\n                      close-ups.\n  auto_capped_768   - same, but clamped to 768 (H3's native short edge, and a\n                      sane VRAM ceiling). This is what ships here.\n\ncanvas_w / canvas_h are WIRED into the H3 node's width/height on purpose. In the auto modes the tracker chooses the size, and if the H3 node disagrees the latent shapes differ and injection refuses. Do not retype them by hand.\n\nWatch the tracker's report for \"magnification < 1.0x\": that means the crop is being DOWNSCALED into the canvas and real detail is being thrown away. Raise the canvas, or skip the clip if it is close-up throughout.\n\nCost scales with canvas AREA x frames, so 768 is 2.25x the latent tokens of 512."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
