   "title": "Stitch + SAM mask",
   "properties": {
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "STITCH - SAM mask variant\n\nREQUIRES ComfyUI-Impact-Pack (for SAMLoader) and a SAM model in models/sams/.\nIf you would rather not add that dependency, use H3_Face_Refine.json\ninstead - it uses a rect mask and needs neither.\n\nKEY POINT: the wide crop exists to give the SAMPLER CONTEXT. It is NOT what gets\npasted. Only the face region composites; everything else keeps its original pixels.\n\nThe 'masks' input OVERRIDES paste_region with a true face-shaped mask, so the blend\nfalls on the jaw and hairline instead of an arbitrary rectangle.\n\nFEATHER IS IN SOURCE PIXELS. With a SAM mask use a SMALL feather (4-8; this graph\nships 8). A rect mask needs far more (~24).\n\nSAM MASKS THE INPUT, NEVER THE OUTPUT. The mask node takes the TRACKER's crops, not\nthe decoded result - the same way FaceDetailer computes its mask from the source\nimage. Mask the generated result instead and, if the model nudges the face inward,\nthe mask traces the NEW smaller silhouette while the original face pokes out past it\n- most visibly the nose on profile shots. It is also cheaper: no dependency on the\nsampler, so SAM need not be resident alongside the video model.\n\nWORTH KNOWING: a rect mask often BEATS this. SAM traces the face tightly, so any\ndrift in the refined face lands right on the silhouette. A slightly looser rect puts\nthe seam in hair and background where it reads far less."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
