   "title": "READ ME FIRST",
   "properties": {
    "ue_properties": {
     "widget_ue_connectable": {},
     "version": "7.8",
     "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
    }
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "WHY THIS EXISTS\n\nMiniMax H3 renders faces poorly when the head is a SMALL FRACTION OF THE FRAME. That is a property of head-size-in-frame, not of resolution - it persists at 720p and above.\n\nSo no upscaler fixes it. SeedVR2 and friends sharpen what is already there; they cannot synthesise facial structure that was never generated.\n\nThe fix: crop to the face so it fills the frame, let H3 re-generate it at LOW denoise so it stays frame-aligned, then composite back."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
